From 95decfefb82e64f6e391b7e2a18acd4d69df28cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:05:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Desktop: bound remote request time so a slow link
 can't wedge the hub connection

On a ~1-2 Mbps link (2026-11-12, MacBook on a guest network, Tailscale via
DERP) the Desktop held 51 sockets to the hub tunnel, so every new request
queued in the 50-socket JSON Agent with no bound: `req.setTimeout` is an idle
timer that starts only once a socket is assigned, and a trickling response
never trips it. A 10 s /api/health dispatch probe ran 227 s and tore down
healthy tunnels, and a down-gate trial held its slot for 3.5 min while every
hub call failed fast with "reconnect in progress".

1. fetchJson / fetchPublicJson: a total per-attempt deadline
   (startRequestDeadline in api-transport.ts) started before http.request,
   covering Agent queue wait, connect and response. On expiry the promise
   rejects with the existing "Timed out connecting to Hermes backend after
   Nms" error first, then the request is destroyed, so down-gate and retry
   classification are unchanged. The idle timeout is kept.
2. Down gate: a trial (connect + request) gets a 20 s total deadline
   (REMOTE_DOWN_TRIAL_DEADLINE_MS). On expiry the owning trial calls
   markDown (escalates the backoff, frees the slot) and rejects with a
   timeout; the abandoned work no longer owns the trial.
3. The dispatch probe (ensureHealthyPooledRemoteBackendForDispatch) asks for
   pool 'probe': a dedicated keep-alive Agent with maxSockets 2, so a
   saturated JSON pool can't fail the probe.

Tests (each RED on the pre-fix code): a request queued behind a full Agent
and a trickling response reject by the deadline; the probe answers while the
JSON pool holds 50 hung requests to the same server; a trial whose connect or
request hangs frees the slot by its deadline and the next trial runs; the
dispatch probe requests the probe pool.

multipartBody moves from main.ts to api-transport.ts unchanged, offsetting
main.ts's FILE_LINES growth.

Card: t_01a1d3b1a4a9d420 (found on t_01a1d36e8c0752f8).
